      "content": "To quantify community cohesion, you could analyze the temporal stability of local businesses (median operational tenure) alongside peer-to-peer lending repayment default rates within those zip codes. Incorporating high-resolution, anonymized census tract flow data for short-term rental occupancy versus year-round resident turnover can effectively distinguish transient networks from stable long-term communities. Since behavior is a strong proxy for social ties, tracing cross-neighborhood pawn shop transaction frequency or utility bill collection consistency across adjacent blocks often serves as a surprisingly robust indicator of embeddedness.",
